---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { site } from '../data/business';

const title = 'Electrical projects in Kempston';
const description = 'Hurley Electrical does not publish made-up case studies. This page covers the Singer Way workshop, emergency lighting servicing, and the jobs customers have described.';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Projects', path: '/projects' },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/projects" crumbs={crumbs}>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Projects"
    title="Work we can point to"
    lede="No invented street names, prices, or before-and-after photos. This is the workshop, the BSI scope, and the jobs named in reviews."
    crumbs={crumbs}
  />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap" style="display:grid;gap:1.2rem">
      <article class="prose-card prose">
        <img src="/images/workshop.webp" width="1600" height="900" alt="Google Street View of the industrial units on Singer Way, Kempston." style="border-radius:14px;width:100%;max-height:420px;object-fit:cover" />
        <p class="kicker">Google Street View</p>
        <h2>The workshop on Singer Way</h2>
        <p>The Google listing for Hurley Electrical does not have a gallery of job photos uploaded by the business. The picture Google shows is Street View of the units on Singer Way, Kempston. That is the picture above.</p>
        <p>The address is 18 Singer Way, Woburn Road Industrial Estate, Kempston, Bedford, MK42 7AE. The estate is on the south side of Kempston, near the A421. Visits are by arrangement. Phone {site.phoneDisplay} before you come, so someone is there to meet you.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="prose-card prose" id="lighting">
        <h2>Emergency lighting servicing</h2>
        <p>This is not a story about one building. It is the scope BSI lists for Hurley Ltd in Kempston, licence {site.bsiLicence}.</p>
        <p>The listing covers maintenance of emergency lighting systems to SP203-4 version 2.2, BS 5266-1:2016, BS EN 1838:2013, and BS EN 50172:2004. In plain words, that is planned checks on the lights that should stay on if the power fails, with the records that go with those checks.</p>
        <p>A Google review also says we check communal lighting for bpha homes, and that lights were left off after a visit. If you manage a block, ask how the test is done and how the lights are left. Read Colin Allen’s review on the reviews page before you decide.</p>
        <p><a href={site.bsiListing}>Open the BSI listing</a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="prose-card prose" id="small-works">
        <h2>Sockets, switches, and fans</h2>
        <p>Teresa Spadaccino’s 2021 Google review thanks Matthew Hurley and Jamie Collins. The review record lists outlet and switch relocation. Katie Dale’s review from October 2021 is logged as outlet and switch installation. Manjit Jakku wrote in February 2022 about extractor fans, and said the explanation was useful.</p>
        <p>Those are the small works we can name without inventing a job sheet. If yours is similar, say so on the form. If it is something else, say that too. We would rather turn a job down than pretend it is on a list.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="prose-card prose">
        <h2>Housing repairs</h2>
        <p>Our old website said we work in partnership with bpha. Colin Allen’s review says we are contractors for bpha and that we carry out repairs. It is also a complaint about communal lighting. We are not turning that into a success story. It is part of the public record, and it belongs next to the praise.</p>
        <p>If you are a tenant, start with the housing association. If you instruct work yourself, call the workshop number on this site.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand />
</Base>
